  <mdb:resourceLineage>
    <mrl:LI_Lineage>
      <mrl:statement>
        <gco:CharacterString>Copied from water_reference_bodies with existing UUIDs and Hylak_id unchanged. Publication schema adds direct geometry/name references and scoped references between distinct accepted names; no identities or geographic assignments changed. Publication repair reorganized self-touching rings in 1 polygons into valid exterior/interior rings. Coordinate sets, boundary point sets, polygon-part counts, IDs and all nongeometry source attributes were preserved. Linework and structure make_valid results agreed. Repair method is recorded per feature; original validity diagnostics remain in the internal audit and original source datasets are unchanged. Public schema omits repeated validity diagnostics and internal processing fields. Original evidence remains in the workflow audit; public IDs, geometry and retained attributes are unchanged. Public schema omits repeated validity diagnostics and internal processing fields. Original evidence remains in the workflow audit; public IDs, geometry and retained attributes are unchanged.</gco:CharacterString>
      </mrl:statement>
      <mrl:source>
        <mrl:LI_Source>
          <mrl:description>
            <gco:CharacterString>HydroLAKES v1.0</gco:CharacterString>
          </mrl:description>
        </mrl:LI_Source>
      </mrl:source>
    </mrl:LI_Lineage>
